message.reasoning:
 need to produce JSON with orders status and payments list, plus orphans.

Given one order PED-1007 amount 1234.50. Statement has one payment line with e2e_id E1000000010001 amount "R$ 1.234,49" which is 1234.49 (since comma decimal). So amount is 1234.49, which is less than order amount 1234.50. It's linked by txid = order id.

Only one e2e_id, no duplicates. No refund lines.

Now compute status: payment amount received distinct transfers sum? For status definitions, they refer to amount received in distinct transfers (gross). Underpaid if less than order amount received. Overpaid if more than order amount. Paid if exactly order amount received at or before expires_at. Late_paid if exactly order amount after expires_at. Refund status if linked payment fully returned by refund line.

In this case amount is less than order amount, so underpaid.

But need to consider rule 9: order of precedence: unpaid, refunded, underpaid, overpaid, late_paid, paid. So underpaid applies.

Now payments list: includes e2e_id strings sorted. Only one: "E1000000010001". So payments: ["E1000000010001"].

Orphans: distinct e2e_ids of payment lines cannot be linked to any order. This line is linked, so none. Orphans empty list.

Now produce JSON:

{
 "orders": {
   "PED-1007": {
     "status": "underpaid",
     "payments": ["E1000000010001"]
   }
 },
 "orphans": []
}

Make sure amounts format correct: status string exactly "underpaid". Payments sorted - single.

